# Build context exclusions for the Layer 4 quota-router node image.
#
# BuildKit reads this file when the Dockerfile is not at the context root:
# it looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile. The
# context itself is the repository root, so without this the transfer
# carries the whole local build tree.
#
# That is not hypothetical here. `target/` reached 120 GB on a machine
# that has run the full workspace test suite, and `COPY . .` would have
# written all of it into the builder layer before cargo was even
# invoked. The `crates/octo-cli/tests/e2e_docker/` image is built from
# the same repository root and carries the equivalent file; this one
# was simply never added, which is why `layer4_2node` had never been
# run end to end.
#
# SCOPE RULE, carried over from that sibling file: only exclude what is
# provably irrelevant AND large. Do not add `cairo/` here — `zk-circuit`
# reads `cairo/src/lib.cairo` at compile time, and excluding it breaks
# dependency resolution with an error that names a path rather than the
# mistake. Prose directories total a few tens of MB against a multi-GB
# context, so excluding them saves nothing and risks the same class of
# failure.

# Build output and the local toolchain cache. By far the largest
# source-tree-adjacent directory.
target/
**/target/

# Version control and CI. `.git` alone is over a gigabyte.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Local virtualenvs and Python caches.
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Agent tooling state and caches. Large, and none of it participates in
# a cargo build.
.claude/
.clinerules/
.agents/
agents/
.cocoindex_code/
.continue/
.cursor/
.gitnexus/
.jcode/
.mimocode/
.opencode/
.openclaude/
.playwright-mcp/

# Local test and analysis scratch output.
live-tests/
check_arc3b/
.octo/
.audit/
.audits/
tarpaulin-report.json
cobertura.xml
*.profraw

# NOT excluded, deliberately: `cairo/` (read by `zk-circuit` at compile
# time), `docs/`, `rfcs/`, `missions/`, `memory/`, `python/`,
# `examples/`, `packaging/`, `pipelines/`, and the root-level crates
# `determin/`, `octo-sync/`, `octo-transport/`, `quota-router/`,
# `quota-router-e2e-tests/`, `sync-e2e-tests/`. Several are read by
# build scripts; the rest are small.
